--Power BI Pop-Out Filter Pane Using Bookmarks
--For when your page gets too crowded with filters, create a pop-out filter pane.

Step 1: Create the Filter Panel
1.1 Insert a Background Shape

Navigate to:  Insert → Shapes → Rounded Rectangle (or whichever shape you like)
--format the shape to your liking

1.2 Add Your Slicers
Create slicers for your filters and position them inside the shape you created in Step 1.  
Example slicers:Region, Site, Product, Department etc

Step 2: Create the Open Filter Button
Navigate to:  Insert → Buttons → Blank
Position the button outside the panel.
Label it: "Open filter pane" or something to that effect.  This button will display the filter panel.

Step 3: Create the Close Filter Button
Insert another button.
Label it: Close Filter Pane
Place it inside the filter panel.
This button will hide the filter panel.

Step 4: Open the Selection and Bookmark Panes
Navigate to:  View → Selection
AND
View → Bookmarks
You need BOTH open

You should now have
Selection Pane:
Open Button
Close Button
Slicer 1
Slicer 2
Slicer 3
Background Shape
Bookmark Pane:  empty for now
These two panes are required for the pop-out panel functionality.

Step 5: Group the Filter Objects
In the Selection Pane:
Hold Ctrl and select:
Close Button
Slicer 1
Slicer 2
Slicer 3
Background Shape

Then Right-click -> Group -> Rename the group to "Filter Pane"
Your Selection Pane now looks like:
Selection
-----------
Open Button

Filter Pane
  Background Shape
  Region Slicer
  Audit Result Slicer
  Audit Body Slicer
  Close Button

Step 6: Create the CLOSED Bookmark
Hide the Filter Pane
In the Selection Pane:
Click the eye icon next to Filter Pane

The panel disappears.  Only the Open button should remain visible.

Create Bookmark:
Open the Bookmarks Pane.
Select: ADD
Rename the bookmark to "Closed"

Bookmark Settings
Select the three dots beside the bookmark.
Choose:
☐ Data
☑ Display
☑ Current Page
Data should generally be OFF so that slicer selections are not reset when opening or closing the pane.

Step 7: Create the OPEN Bookmark
Return to the Selection Pane.
Click the eye icon beside Filter Pane.  The panel becomes visible again.

Create Open Bookmark
Select: ADD
Rename the bookmark to "Open"
Bookmark Settings
Configure:
☐ Data
☑ Display
☑ Current Page
AGAIN: Data = OFF

Step 8: Connect the Buttons to the Bookmarks
Open Filter Button
Select: Open Filter Pane
Navigate to: Format Pane → Action
Turn Action ON.
Configure:
Type = Bookmark
Bookmark = Open

Example:

Action
------
ON

Type:
Bookmark

Bookmark:
Open
----
Close Filter Button
Select:  Close Filter Pane
Navigate to: Format Pane → Action
Configure:
Type = Bookmark
Bookmark = Closed

Example:
Action
------
ON

Type:
Bookmark

Bookmark:
Closed

Professional Version:   For a more polished result:

Move the panel partially off-screen.
Create an Open bookmark with panel visible.
Create a Closed bookmark with panel hidden outside the page.
Use icons instead of text buttons.
Add a semi-transparent dark overlay behind the panel.
